file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scope_rank.sh landed -- what each map row saves, and which row to write next
file tools/fixtures/s/scope_match.sh landed -- the map matcher written once, sourced by runner and ranking
file tools/fixtures/i/index_shelf_repair.sh landed, and first resident on the fault the recovery itself carried
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scope_map.sh the row that grew session-logs/date/, so a scoped pass stops skipping the shelf's guard
file construction/REDS.md %540 seated at the stamp the parked lap booked, headline recounted
file construction/ITINERARY.md the landing account, the flake family's third guard, the orphaned-lock repair
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260907.md the duplicate dropped by hand, the inversion sorted by the tool
scope one Aether lap -- a parked lap landed whole, its row renumbered on the fetch, and the shelf red closed by the instrument the same stash carried
status GREEN -- scope_rank 56 behaviors, index_row_bound 24, index_row_bound_scan verdict=ok, spine next_free read after fetch
recommend keep-going -- the ranking now names the four costliest unmapped guards on disk (declared_ceiling 71s, width_check 69s, lantern_face 56s, borrowed_number 53s), and writing their map rows is the first work that spends the instrument this lap landed.
